.TH HATIMHANE 1 "October 2026" "Hatimhane 0.2.0"
.SH NAME
hatimhane \- mosque and Quran reading group management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hatimhane
.RB [ --config-dir " directory" ]
.I command
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run HTTP administration, public JSON publishing and scheduling in one service.
.TP
.B owner --username name [--password-file path] [--reset]
Create an owner account. Without a password file, prompt securely on the terminal.
Reset clears two-factor authentication and revokes existing sessions.
.TP
.B import --json path --slug uri [--mosque-name name]
Import the earlier single-mosque JSON format into a new mosque and group.
.TP
.B check
Validate configuration and connect to the database. Creates the initial schema.
.SH FILES
/etc/hatimhane.d/*.toml are loaded in lexical order.
Data and public snapshots are stored under /var/lib/hatimhane.
.SH SECURITY
Serve behind an HTTPS reverse proxy. Public requests use snapshots, not database queries.
No default account or password is provided.
.SH AUTHOR
Oktay Aktoğan
